-- Names with no section in front of them are quoted the way L4 writes them in
-- source, as they are under a section (overnight card O6, 2026-10-11; found in
-- review): a mixfix rule `scaled by` and a rule `two words` at the top of a
-- file print as `` `scaled by` `` and `` `two words` ``. The input is not quoted.

GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      factor IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2
GIVETH A NUMBER
base `scaled by` factor MEANS base TIMES factor

GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`two words` MEANS `the rate` TIMES base

@export default Combine
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE combine IS (`scaled by` WITH base IS n) PLUS (`two words` WITH base IS n)
